From 63514b4019c9b515c274cac5f2fd82728d293ccc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:26:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] drm: apple: Map a RAM page for bw-scratch in Dashboard
 mode

On t8122 (M3) the devicetree has apple,bw-scratch but no
apple,bw-doorbell, so the DCP firmware runs its RT bandwidth handling in
"Dashboard" mode. It asks for the pmgr dashboard page through the
map_reg callback (D411) and the driver maps the MMIO page into dart-dcp
with dma_map_resource().

The firmware's only write through that mapping is a 64-bit zero to the
bw-scratch offset (0x908) on power-off. dart-dcp rejects it:

  apple-dart 28d30c000.iommu: translation fault: status:0x90540008
  stream:5 ... NO PTE FOR IOVA at 0x10fffdfc908

(FILL_REGION | NO_PTE), the DCP crashes and the display never comes
back after the first screen blank / DPMS off.

At the fault the page tables, TTBR/TCR and the iBoot-programmed APF
slices (which cover 0x2d03c0000-0x2d03effff) are intact, and a DART TLB
flush before power-off does not help. The locked access-region
registers only cover DRAM, which may be why the DART refuses to fill an
MMIO target; that could not be tested because they ignore writes.

Hand the firmware a RAM page instead of the dashboard page in Dashboard
mode. pmgr no longer sees the firmware's final zero write; the
dashboard already reads zero at power-on, so nothing else is lost.

Tested on MacBook Air M3 (J613), DCP 14.7: 4 boots with 3 blank/unblank
cycles each and a normal Hyprland session with DPMS off/on, no DART
fault and no DCP crash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017YMqWu7A3VwEYtHaA1TusK
---
 linux/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/linux/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c b/linux/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
index a41db29..058575b 100644
--- a/linux/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/linux/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -472,8 +472,25 @@ static struct DCP_FW_NAME(dcp_map_reg_resp) dcpep_cb_map_reg(struct apple_dcp *d
 	} else {
 		struct resource *rsrc = dcp->disp_registers[req->index];
 #if DCP_FW_VER >= DCP_FW_VERSION(13, 2, 0)
-		dma_addr_t dva = dma_map_resource(dcp->dev, rsrc->start, resource_size(rsrc),
-						  DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL, 0);
+		dma_addr_t dva;
+
+		/*
+		 * In "Dashboard" RT bandwidth mode (bw-scratch without a
+		 * bw-doorbell, e.g. t8122) the firmware's only write through
+		 * this mapping is a 64-bit zero to the pmgr dashboard on
+		 * power-off. dart-dcp rejects it (FILL_REGION|NO_PTE) and the
+		 * DCP crashes, so hand the firmware a RAM page instead.
+		 */
+		if (dcp->disp_bw_scratch_index && !dcp->disp_bw_doorbell_index &&
+		    req->index == dcp->disp_bw_scratch_index) {
+			if (!dmam_alloc_coherent(dcp->dev, resource_size(rsrc),
+						 &dva, GFP_KERNEL))
+				dva = DMA_MAPPING_ERROR;
+		} else {
+			dva = dma_map_resource(dcp->dev, rsrc->start,
+					       resource_size(rsrc),
+					       DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL, 0);
+		}
 		WARN_ON(dva == DMA_MAPPING_ERROR);
 #endif
 
